# SPIRE local-deploy environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in the values you
# want passed through to the backend container by docker compose.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up -d --build
#
# Anything you leave blank or commented out keeps the existing default —
# SPIRE will run fine without these set.

# --- Pilot feedback → GitHub issues ----------------------------------------
# When SPIRE_GITHUB_TOKEN is set, the in-app feedback drawer (Shift+F)
# creates a GitHub issue on SPIRE_GITHUB_REPO in addition to landing the
# feedback in the local audit chain.
#
# Recommended: a fine-grained Personal Access Token scoped to ONE repo
# (jeranaias/spire) with these permissions, nothing else:
#   - Repository access: Only select repositories → jeranaias/spire
#   - Permissions → Repository → Issues: Read and write
#   - Expiration: 90 days (renew at the start of each pilot rotation)
#
# Generate at: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# Tokens look like: github_pat_11ABCD…
SPIRE_GITHUB_TOKEN=
SPIRE_GITHUB_REPO=jeranaias/spire

# --- At-rest encryption ----------------------------------------------------
# Enables AES-256 encryption of the SQLite audit chain. Strongly recommended
# for any deployment that leaves a Marine's laptop. Leave unset for dev only.
# SPIRE_DB_PASSPHRASE=change-me-in-production
